Discussion

The purpose of this study was to understand how distractive the use of HMD-based AR system is. The use of AR system was compared to real and virtual setups to understand real-world awareness, perceived workload and the experience in the RV continuum. In addition, implications to the user studies are suggested and limitations and future work are addressed.
Conclusions

The use of AR systems is increasing in industry. However, there are still some concerns that AR systems may distract the user and create safety risks. The purpose of this study was to understand if the use of a HMD-based AR system distract users’ awareness of the environment. The experience was evaluated in a laboratory study by comparing three different test setups: real system, AR system and VR system.

